WEBVTT

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.910
Wish to blink. Now would be the time.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.340
Just do it if you're gonna do it.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:31.740
Are you all right, John?

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.520
Yeah. Sure. No problem. Happens all the time. Needle in the eye. No sweat.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.840
All finished. Which of you is next?

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.200
You go next.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.000
I told you I'm not participating.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.590
But, uh...

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.570
Park it in the chair and get this over with so we can get out of here.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.050
You're not comfortable here, my dear. Is it my reputation?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.950
It is your reputation, Namtar, that led us here.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.780
Yes, it certainly is an honor to meet such a learned scientist as yourself.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.220
and to take part in his grand experiments.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.360
I'm sure that this is worth a stick in the eye, right?

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.400
You do want to go home, don't you, John?

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.970
Namta may have data that Moyer is lacking,

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.790
data that we're desperately in need of.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.940
You're looking for a DNA sample, right?

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.800
Can't you just take a skin scraping...

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.460
If I were working nearly at the double helix level, yes,

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.920
but to provide you with the information you desire...

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.720
Is this going to take long?

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:29.900
Moment.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.340
Mere moments.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:38.500
Cornata.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:39.730
Your assistance.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:01:59.970
Will do each of you...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.900
in turn, but beautiful Zan, I have chosen to do yours first.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.880
A genetic database holds information on nearly 11 million species.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:57.450
It is simple for me to take a genetic sampling of a particular being and pinpoint the location of its origin.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:29.500
Me too, right?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:36.760
provide you with a genetic map to your home world a map that will allow you to make the journey and

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:44.750
avoid any peacekeeper jurisdictions along the way that is what you came here for isn't it i'm

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:58.720
delighted i have the very thing you each desire so strongly and now my price

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.820
Yes, I believe I told you when I first contacted you that our resources are somewhat, well, limited.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:09.480
You arrived here aboard a Leviathan ship, did you not?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.000
You want our ship?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:15.550
My interest isn't in your ship, but in your ship's pilot.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.110
What do you want with him?

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:24.100
My research will be greatly enhanced by genetic material from such an extraordinary species.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.890
You mean a sample like it must?

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:28.930
A sample, yes.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.850
But I'm afraid I'm going to need a bit more than I asked of you.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.120
How much more?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:41.840
I will require one of your pilot's arms.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.300
John Crichton, an astronaut.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:04:59.980
Radiation.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.680
and I got shot through a wormhole.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.500
Lost in some distant part of the universe on a ship.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.080
A living ship full of strange alien life forms.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:09.720
Help, help.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:10.600
Listen, please.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.010
Is there anybody out there who can hear me?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.440
Being hunted by an insane military commander

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.900
doing everything I can.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.770
I'm just looking for a way home.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.560
Don't you want to analyze it before?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.430
We're usually so careful about these things.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.210
Neurotically careful.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:12.230
What's wrong?

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:15.100
I'm actually on that one.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.270
You know, you're no worse off than you were a couple of arms ago.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.810
So Namthar didn't have Earth on his data stores.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.220
11 million species.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.160
Eleven million, and he couldn't at least narrow it down for me?

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.240
I mean, sure, he can't pinpoint the exact location,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.020
but am I even in the neighborhood here?

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.590
I should have pinpointed the others, no problem.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:44.630
What's your problem?

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.460
You know, you didn't even let him poke you in the eye.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.810
You don't even know if he's got your home world in his big ball of wonders.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:53.650
Have you forgotten?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.900
You and the others are trying to get home, avoiding peacekeeper territories.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:06:59.980
My home...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:15.620
is peacekeeper territories it's just that i can't ever go back there ever have you forgotten

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:22.960
nam tar's demand i mean unless pilot volunteers one of his arms we're all gonna be blessed and

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:29.960
out here together in about one hour one hour you saw the looks on the others faces makes you think

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.960
they're going to wait for pilot to volunteer at anything what do you think you're doing please i

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:42.120
implore you just listen to what how dare you i'm tar has offered something that we cannot obtain

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:47.690
anywhere else think about somebody else for a shame i will help ease your pain

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.220
You have upheld our end of the bargain, Nantar.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.020
Yes, you have. Splendidly.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.840
And I will uphold mine.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.420
It will take me a short while to load the cartographs to all three of your homeworlds into the crystal.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.080
How much of a while?

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:29.700
I sense you don't completely...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.380
Trust me, but you needn't worry.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.900
The crystal will be delivered to your ship shortly.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.220
We will await your messenger.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:46.740
Cornata!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.760
Let us hope the pilot DNA shows better results.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:26.960
You are finished.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:38.090
I said you are finished. Don't concern yourself, Crichton. I will be fine.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:42.200
My species has superior regenerative capabilities.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:47.370
So you, um, you let them cut off one of your arms?

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:52.970
I didn't exactly let them. They have the opportunity to go home.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.200
The drive is very strong.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:59.970
I will never stand you, p-

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.540
how can you not be angry insanely angry when one of my species is bonded to a

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:14.500
leviathan we give our lives to the service of others ship first then those who travel aboard

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:21.570
her no matter what those aboard do to you my species is incapable of space flight on our own

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:28.740
if we wish to journey beyond our home planet this is the trade-off we make for the chance to see the

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.100
Galaxy

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.450
I consider it a perfectly equitable arrangement.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.440
Something to say to us?

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.760
The decision was a hard one.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.110
But it is done.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.970
How could you pilot it?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.710
defenseless imagine from a peacekeeper for a comrade you attacked one of your

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:18.400
own would you do the same to the rest of us course but you have your maps now

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.540
what makes you think you can just take this ship wherever you want to go these

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:27.970
maps are precisely what we've been longing for our way home pilot will not

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.570
help you after what you have done to him

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.400
is a servicer.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.490
You get over it.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.500
I'll see to it.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.890
I know what is troubling you, my dear.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.330
You'll never find your way home.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.260
But please do not deny ourselves.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.210
Our chance to find our own.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:05.830
They're getting their maps.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.660
Pilot says he's going to be okay.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.480
It's only one of his arms.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.660
Hell, he's got four.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.390
I guess that makes you and me the odd man out.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.030
That means they're going home and we're not.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.970
Hey, you know, even with the, um...

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.500
Maps, it's still gonna take him some time to make the trips.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.610
And then it's just you and me.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.720
You know, I'm not entirely useless here, you know.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:46.600
I happen to be learning.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.400
What's the matter?

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.280
They are going home.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.480
And someday, you will too.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:14.160
Sure.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.700
I never find a way home.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.210
I was born a peacekeeper soldier.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:22.790
I've always been one among many.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:28.560
Member of a division, platoon, a unit, team.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:39.600
I've never been on my own, John. Never been alone. Ever.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:47.130
I'll find a way home if I take you with me.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.440
Me on a planet full of billions of you.

00:13:58.660 --> 00:13:59.100
Out!

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:04.480
And again, I mean, that's what I was thinking, getting over it, though.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:09.820
Ah, so sorry.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.060
I came to inform you that the data crystal is on its way.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.380
What is all this?

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:20.400
Hmm, just items that I've procured since our escape to wait us in our bartering.

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:25.260
Of course, when I return home and reclaim my birthright,

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:29.370
awful such as this will no longer be allowed to offend my sight.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.600
A box of food cubes.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:38.510
My emergency supply, in case something came up.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.180
How long have you had these for?

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:47.240
Were they in your possession when we were without food for nearly two weekends?

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.690
You see, something did come up.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.560
If you like them, they're yours.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:56.940
Have not reclaimed your birthright yet, little man.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:04.590
I did not expect Aaron to share our excitement, but Crichton's attitude surprises me.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:08.780
If Nemtar's knowledge had extended to Crichton's pathetic homeworld,

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:12.560
you can wager that he would have offered up his own meme box, useless as they are.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.860
Would you if that had been the price demanded?

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.200
Fortunately, it was not.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.000
Only a female would make light of such a thought.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.640
I was not making light.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.790
And you, what would you have given?

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.730
I would risk my Numa for the chance to go home.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.920
Nemtar has no use for that.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.800
I'm surprised that he has stayed out here in the uncharted territories.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:41.260
His knowledge could bring him great fame and power, even great wealth.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:44.540
It could change the entire basis of astro-navigation.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:47.200
It would change the basis for war.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:55.070
One single prisoner, and you would have the ability to strike at their very heart, their homeland.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:58.990
You would pervert Nam-Tar's genius to a weapon?

00:15:59.400 --> 00:15:59.920
What?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:07.910
somebody will why shouldn't it be me you still feel pain from the needle it's nothing and soon

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:16.430
forgotten once we're on our voyage home on delvia the pilgrim will be just coming to bloom my parents

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:22.800
will be preparing for the festival of predrar there is no need for them to keep my seat vacant

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:28.220
this cycle's festival if you reach there this cycle

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.300
Crystal will be arriving from Nam-Tar within an arm.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.480
I don't doubt, but there are decisions to be made about our course.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:43.770
Without my call to Blade, you would not have been able to give Nam-Tar what he wanted.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.050
I will make the decisions.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:51.450
To suit yourself, but it is not as easy as you wish.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:55.360
This is a time for logic and reason.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.650
Yes, of course, you wish to find yourself at us with.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:03.880
Everyone on the ship, not just Aaron Sohner.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:07.490
What do you suggest?

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.160
Fair compromise.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:30.970
You're angry!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:40.910
There's someone to see you.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.180
I was here earlier.

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:52.680
Of course.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.990
You are looking for my help?

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.490
I wish to participate in your research.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.480
Excellent. What made you change your mind, my dear?

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:16.640
I know that there are other Sabatian colonies beyond the known territory.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:22.680
I want you to find me one where I can fit in.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:27.380
Then we will look for it together.

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:33.910
You understand what I'm about to do.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.380
You'll take some fluid from my eye.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:36.900
Exactly.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:41.450
Remain absolutely still.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:55.330
Only.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:10.960
Is that it?

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:12.330
It is done.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.190
When will I know the result?

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.670
It won't be long at all.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.370
I, of course, will return home first.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:39.870
You.

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:42.970
I bartered for the coordinates to this asteroid.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:45.470
I made the first contact with Namtar.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.190
I struck the deal.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.730
I go home first.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.110
Bargo and I have already spoken.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.670
Whoever's home is the closest.

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:54.050
That is where we will travel to first.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.880
You two have spoken.

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:58.180
Without consulting me.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:19:59.100
What am I?

00:19:59.340 --> 00:19:59.980
Chopped me...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.700
Of course not. I can stomach-chopped millet.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.060
What did you call me?

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:08.980
A blue-ass bitch.

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.820
You guys getting all this?

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.300
