Moya is.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.150
Moya isn't.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:18.740
Pilot, how are you?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.140
The yachts with pleasantries?

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.860
What do you mean Moya isn't assimilating the data?

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.430
Is that her doing or yours?

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.610
I have nothing to do with it.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:29.890
Pilot is right.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:34.400
The data is being processed directly by Moya, but there is too much.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.620
There is a great deal of data, but Moya will just have to...

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.500
Moya can do nothing about it.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.580
It appears your crystal is useless.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:47.670
Lucky for you, you didn't trade anything of real value to get it.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:53.620
We can access one of the maps, but only if we destroy the other two.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:57.720
Well, we'll just go to Namtar and ask him for three individual crystals.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.980
If Namtar for further help, what will he...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.020
demand of us then if he should ask for it what body part are you willing to offer your eminence

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.460
do you think you are doing

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:51.920
There's some major crap going down here.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:54.290
Not so loud.

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:55.400
Fine.

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:57.740
Look, we may have a real problem.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.980
The map thing, the Amtar's map.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.460
Well, Larry, Curly, and Moe just found out they can only use one of the maps.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:04.680
Two of them ain't going nowhere.

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:07.180
It's like a regular family feud up there.

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:09.810
You sweating?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.340
This isn't a Sebastian thing, is it?

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:15.320
It's not a Sebastian thing.

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.020
Oh, you gotta give me a clue here, man.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:22.300
Is this something new or is this just your usual PMSP from the military?

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:23.020
Frel you.

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:45.020
Mr. Luxon, the crystal is well hidden.

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:49.300
It will remain so until you and Zion are ready to listen to reason.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:51.780
Reason being that we return you to Hyneria.

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:53.780
That's the very definition of reason.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:55.640
I'll find the damn crystal myself.

00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:58.440
No, I assure you, you won't.

00:22:58.740 --> 00:22:59.980
I have places in this...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.940
that even the Peacekeeper Senthounds couldn't detect.

00:23:04.990 --> 00:23:06.510
If you return to Hyneria,

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:09.070
you will want to wrest your throne from your cousin.

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:10.800
And I will.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:13.180
But your cousin is in control of your armies.

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.170
He himself is probably heavily guarded.

00:23:16.430 --> 00:23:18.990
My paliscentries are inferior to none.

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:21.370
His paliscentries.

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:25.520
However, if you side with me against Zan

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:27.260
to return to my home world first,

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:29.960
imagine returning to your...

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:33.660
with a whole contingent of Luxon warriors at your command.

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:35.060
But you're a fugitive.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.420
Your own people imprisoned you.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:41.830
My leaders imprisoned me, not my people.

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:47.240
